<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Erfurt Union</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1849–1850</span> · Also known as Prussian Union plan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erfurt">Erfurt</a> Union was a Prussian attempt in 1849–1850 to unite the German states, excluding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>, in a federation under Prussian leadership after King Frederick William IV refused the imperial crown offered by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankfurt-parliament">Frankfurt Parliament</a>. A union parliament met in Erfurt in spring 1850, but Austrian and Russian opposition forced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> to abandon the project in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punctation-of-olmutz">Punctation of Olmütz</a> in November 1850.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/erfurt-union.jpg" alt="Erfurt Union" width="320" height="324" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ziko · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Erfurter_Union_zur_Zeit_des_Unionsparlaments.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
